  "version": 1,
  "name": "Two-storey house with kitchen, living and dining rooms below and two bedrooms above",
  "units": "m",
  "meta": {
    "source": "image",
    "scale_note": "The plan has no printed dimensions or room areas, so I used the standard door width of 0.85 m as a last resort. The hall door chord measures about 78 px and the WC door about 67 px, which gives about 90 px per metre. The house comes out at about 9.0 x 5.9 m. This is a rough estimate with moderate-to-low certainty.",
    "notes": "Wall coordinates are centerlines read from a hand-drawn sketch, so they are approximate. Both floors are assumed to have the same outline. The kitchen and living room are open to each other, as are the living and dining rooms. Several window positions on the right wall and on the upper floor are guesses, and I left out the ones I could not read. Door hinge sides are not set. Floor heights are not stated, so I left level elevation out. Stair steps are counted from the step lines, about 12 per flight."
  },
